DESCRIPTION:Organizer: OCPL - Tustin Branch\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mont
 hs\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nCelebrate Filipino American Heritage Month a
 t Tustin Library with a special author visit!\n\nMichelle Sterling is an a
 uthor\, photographer and speech-language pathologist whose picture books i
 nclude When Lola Visits\, A Sweet New Year for Ren\, and Maribel’s Year 
 and Riding Through Rice Fields. Many of her stories are inspired by her he
 ritage\, family traditions and her love of gastronomy and food history. Sh
 e lives in Southern California with her family.\n\nLimited complimentary b
 ooks available\, while supplies last\, courtesy of the Tustin Friends of t
 he Library.\n\nNo registration required\, all ages welcome. Early arrival 
 suggested.\n\nFor more information\, call 714-544-7725 or email ocpl.tusti
 n@occr.ocgov.com\\n\\nMore info: https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/17544528
